 artifact request\n  paths (resolving the parent experiment of an artifact path to its workspace assignment) in the\n  artifacts-only context.\n- Integration tests exercising workspace resolution from artifact request paths with stores\n  uninitialized, including the S3-standard `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` layout.\n- Regression coverage that the tracking server's non-artifact workspace resolution is unchanged.\n- Version compatibility of the plugin release consumed by the MLflow server image with the\n  combined-flag server behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The plugin's workspace resolution initializes in a server context where tracking and model\n  registry stores are not initialized, demonstrated by an executable test (entry-point load,\n  workspace store construction, and mapping lookup without store initialization).\n- Experiment-to-workspace mapping resolved from artifact request paths (S3-standard layout) returns\n  the correct workspace assignment.\n- Integrated with the workspace-aware artifacts-only serving capability, requests that fail\n  workspace validation are denied (HTTP 403) and requests from workspace members are served.\n- The tracking server's non-artifact workspace resolution behavior is unchanged (regression tests\n  green).\n- The plugin version consumed by the MLflow server build is verified compatible with combined-flag\n  artifacts-only serving.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P1, raised to P0 by inheritance): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in\n  the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — delivered under outcome A of\n  the gating investigation (verification and integration scope).\n- Supports HLR-2 (P0): the plugin's resolution is the delegation target of the server's workspace\n  validation of artifact requests.\n\n## Notes\n\n- This branch epic exists only if the workspace-resolution initialization-dependency investigation\n  determines outcome A (decoupled). If the invest