d\n  `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` layout.\n- Integration tests exercising the independent initialization path in the artifacts-only context\n  (resolution with stores uninitialized).\n- Regression coverage that the tracking server's non-artifact workspace resolution is unchanged by\n  the refactoring.\n- Version compatibility of the plugin release consumed by the MLflow server image with the\n  combined-flag server behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Workspace resolution initializes via the independent initialization path in a server context where\n  tracking and model registry stores are not initialized, demonstrated by an executable test.\n- Experiment-to-workspace mapping resolved from artifact request paths (S3-standard layout) returns\n  the correct workspace assignment through the refactored path.\n- The tracking server's non-artifact workspace resolution behavior is unchanged by the refactoring\n  (regression tests green).\n- Integrated with the workspace-aware artifacts-only serving capability, requests that fail\n  workspace validation are denied (HTTP 403) and requests from workspace members are served.\n- The plugin version consumed by the MLflow server build is verified compatible with combined-flag\n  artifacts-only serving.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P1, raised to P0 by inheritance): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in\n  the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — delivered under outcome B of\n  the gating investigation (refactoring scope).\n- Supports HLR-2 (P0): the plugin's resolution is the delegation target of the server's workspace\n  validation of artifact requests.\n\n## Notes\n\n- This branch epic exists only if the workspace-resolution initialization-dependency investigation\n  determines outcome B (coupled). If the investigation finds the resolution decoupled (outcome A),\n  this refactoring is unnecessary and the plugin work reduces to verification and integration per\n  the 