xisting API contracts, CLI arguments, or configuration keys change meaning.\n- Test coverage: delegation active (artifact operations routed to the configured dedicated\n  instance), delegation absent (current behavior), and interaction with workspace-aware\n  artifacts-only serving (delegated requests remain subject to workspace validation at the\n  dedicated instance).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A tracking server configured with the artifact-delegation configuration delegates artifact\n  operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, verified by artifact requests being served\n  through the dedicated instance.\n- A tracking server without the delegation configuration serves artifact traffic exactly as before\n  (current behavior preserved, regression suite green).\n- The configuration is consumable by the operator's existing configuration-propagation mechanisms\n  for the main tracking deployment.\n- Artifact requests delegated to the dedicated instance remain subject to workspace validation at\n  that instance (end-to-end through the split topology).\n- The configuration surface is documented for administrators of multi-tenant deployments.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only\n  instance — this epic delivers the server-side half of that routing under outcome B of the gating\n  investigation (the operator-side routing configuration is delivered by the split-server operator\n  topology work).\n\n## Notes\n\n- This branch epic exists only if the split-server routing design investigation determines outcome B\n  (the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations). Under outcome\n  A (route-level traffic splitting at the Gateway/HTTPRoute layer), no tracking-server change is\n  needed and this work falls away.\n- Builds on the workspace-aware artifacts-only serving capability delivered by the server-side\n  combined-flag work; delegated artifact requests are validated at the dedicated instance by that\n  capability.\n- Component mapping: canonical Jira component `MLflow`.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":79777,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aacdbd101d79c014","agent_id":"ac3af399cc79681ac","session_id":"16006724-b396-4d55-996f-e395dcbbe214","uuid":"d26825b9-2875-4bdd-85c5-3fe16d789e69","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:38:23.533Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
