{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b414df5737265dbb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-A-E005\n3\ttitle: Verify and integrate plugin workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the workspace-resolution initialization-dependency investigation\n16\t    instead finds resolution coupled to full tracking-server initialization (outcome\n17\t    B), the verification-and-integration scope of this branch is rewritten as the\n18\t    independent-initialization-path refactoring captured in the outcome-B branch plan\n19\t    for the plugin.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: -1\n26\t  external_dependency: 0\n27\t  human_process_gates: -1\n28\t  repo_access: 0\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 3\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Verify and integrate plugin workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tBranch epic — outcome A of the workspace-resolution initialization-dependency investigation\n41\t(decoupled): the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin's workspace resolution initializes and\n42\tresolves experiment-to-workspace mapping without tracking or model registry stores. This epic\n43\tverifies that behavior in the artifacts-only server context and extends the plugin where needed so\n44\tworkspace resolution functions correctly for artifact requests, without changing the plugin's\n45\tbehavior for the tracking server's non-artifact operations.\n46\t\n47\tThe plugin is registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by\n48\t`WorkspaceStoreRegistry`; it already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking\n49\tserver's non-artifact operations. This epic makes that resolution work when driven from artifact\n50\trequest paths in a server where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The\n51\tkube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup are unchanged — authentication at\n52\tthe ingress level works identically for both the tracking server and the artifacts-only instance.\n53\t\n54\t## Scope\n55\t\n56\t- Verification that the plugin's workspace resolution initializes in a server context where tracking\n57\t  and model registry stores are not initialized (entry-point load via `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`,\n58\t  workspace store construction, mapping lookup), per the investigation's outcome-A determination.\n59\t- Extension, where needed, of the plugin's resolution so it can be driven from artifact request\n60\t  paths (resolving the parent experiment of an artifact path to its workspace assignment) in the\n61\t  artifacts-only context.\n62\t- Integration tests exercising workspace resolution from artifact request paths with stores\n63\t  uninitialized, including the S3-standard `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` layout.\n64\t- Regression coverage that the tracking server's non-artifact workspace resolution is unchanged.\n65\t- Version compatibility of the plugin release consumed by the MLflow server image with the\n66\t  combined-flag server behavior.\n67\t\n68\t## Acceptance Criteria\n69\t\n70\t- The plugin's workspace resolution initializes in a server context where tracking and model\n71\t  registry stores are not initialized, demonstrated by an executable test (entry-point load,\n72\t  workspace store construction, and mapping lookup without store initialization).\n73\t- Experiment-to-workspace mapping resolved from artifact request paths (S3-standard layout) returns\n74\t  the correct workspace assignment.\n75\t- Integrated with the workspace-aware artifacts-only serving capability, requests that fail\n76\t  workspace validation are denied (HTTP 403) and requests from workspace members are served.\n77\t- The tracking server's non-artifact workspace resolution behavior is unchanged (regression tests\n78\t  green).\n79\t- The plugin version consumed by the MLflow server build is verified compatible with combined-flag\n80\t  artifacts-only serving.\n81\t\n82\t## HLR Traceability\n83\t\n84\t- HLR-7 (P1, raised to P0 by inheritance): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in\n85\t  the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — delivered under outcome A of\n86\t  the gating investigation (verification and integration scope).\n87\t- Supports HLR-2 (P0): the plugin's resolution is the delegation target of the server's workspace\n88\t  validation of artifact requests.\n89\t\n90\t## Notes\n91\t\n92\t- This branch epic exists only if the workspace-resolution initialization-dependency investigation\n93\t  determines outcome A (decoupled). If the investigation instead finds the resolution coupled to\n94\t  full tracking-server initialization (outcome B), this epic's scope is rewritten as the\n95\t  independent-initialization-path refactoring captured in the outcome-B branch plan for the plugin.\n96\t- Component mapping: canonical Jira component `MLflow`; the work targets the\n97\t  `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` package (no separate canonical entry; `MLflow` is the closest\n98\t  canonical name).\n99\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab7e53c773eaf783","agent_id":"ab7cb31b598d9c582","session_id":"16006724-b396-4d55-996f-e395dcbbe214","uuid":"0afb884b-f7da-4d74-b121-4039dd243d6e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:41:52.719Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b414df5737265dbb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"co