on into an independent initialization path within the\n45\tplugin.\"\n46\t\n47\tThe refactor preserves the plugin's existing behavior for the tracking server's non-artifact\n48\toperations. The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup are unchanged.\n49\t\n50\t## Scope\n51\t\n52\t- Refactor the plugin per the factoring plan produced by the gating investigation: decouple\n53\t  workspace resolution (entry-point loading, workspace store construction, experiment-to-workspace\n54\t  lookup) from the tracking server's full initialization path, following the investigation's\n55\t  identified touch points.\n56\t- Provide an independent initialization path usable by an artifacts-only server that initializes\n57\t  only the workspace provider.\n58\t- Extend resolution as needed so it can be driven from artifact request paths (resolving the parent\n59\t  experiment of an artifact path to its workspace assignment), including the S3-standard\n60\t  `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` layout.\n61\t- Integration tests exercising the independent initialization path in the artifacts-only context\n62\t  (resolution with stores uninitialized).\n63\t- Regression coverage that the tracking server's non-artifact workspace resolution is unchanged by\n64\t  the refactoring.\n65\t- Version compatibility of the plugin release consumed by the MLflow server image with the\n66\t  combined-flag server behavior.\n67\t\n68\t## Acceptance Criteria\n69\t\n70\t- Workspace resolution initializes via the independent initialization path in a server context where\n71\t  tracking and model registry stores are not initialized, demonstrated by an executable test.\n72\t- Experiment-to-workspace mapping resolved from artifact request paths (S3-standard layout) returns\n73\t  the correct workspace assignment through the refactored path.\n74\t- The tracking server's non-artifact workspace resolution behavior is unchanged by the refactoring\n75\t  (regression tests green).\n76\t- Integrated with the workspace-aware artifacts-only serving capability, requests that fail\n77\t  workspace validation are denied (HTTP 403) and requests from workspace members are served.\n78\t- The plugin version consumed by the MLflow server build is verified compatible with combined-flag\n79\t  artifacts-only serving.\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- HLR-7 (P1, raised to P0 by inheritance): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in\n84\t  the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — delivered under outcome B of\n85\t  the gating investigation (refactoring scope).\n86\t- Supports HLR-2 (P0): the plugin's resolution is the delegation target of the server's workspace\n87\t  validation of artifact requests.\n88\t\n89\t## Notes\n90\t\n91\t- This branch epic exists only if the workspace-resolution initialization-dependency investigation\n92\t  determines outcome B (coupled). If the investigation finds the resolution decoupled (outcome A),\n93\t  this refactoring is unnecessary and the plugin work reduces to verification and integration per\n94\t  the outcome-A branch plan.\n95\t- The refactoring's exact scope follows the factoring plan delivered by the gating investigation;\n96\t  this epic does not pre-design the refactor's internal structure.\n97\t- Component mapping: canonical Jira component `MLflow`; the work targets the\n98\t  `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` package (no separate canonical entry; `MLflow` is the closest\n99\t  canonical name).\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab7e53c773eaf783","agent_id":"ab7cb31b598d9c582","session_id":"16006724-b396-4d55-996f-e395dcbbe214","uuid":"09efe486-f3de-4439-a78a-22c6e54eaec4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:41:53.438Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1e7e034cc3f9d95","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
