th directions, and the three Staff Engineer directives (no new flag,\n38\tsplit deployment not config toggle, no SSAR mechanics) are verifiably applied — no epic\n39\tmentions `--artifacts-only-workspace-aware`, `spec.artifactsOnly.workspaceAware`, or\n40\tSelfSubjectAccessReview mechanics. Cross-repo couplings (server ↔ operator ↔ plugin) are\n41\tcorrectly expressed as Rule 13 acceptance-criteria gates rather than blocking edges, keeping\n42\tthe three work streams parallel. One minor issue found (E004 size has no re-split trigger).\n43\t\n44\t## Criterion Details\n45\t\n46\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n47\tAll 8 HLRs map to at least one epic; the traceability matrix is present and complete.\n48\tP0 HLRs 1-4 all land in E003 (P0), with HLR-4 regression additionally covered by E004.\n49\tP1 HLRs 5/6 land in E004 with the conditional server-side half in BRANCH-B-E006; P1 HLR-7\n50\tlands in the E001-gated branch epics, correctly raised to P0 by inheritance since the plugin\n51\twork transitively enables the P0 HLR-2 validation capability. P2 HLR-8 is explicitly bundled\n52\tinto E003 with inline rationale in the matrix row (same denial path as HLR-2/HLR-3; no\n53\tindependent user value) — the compliant bundling shape, not priority collapse. Priority\n54\tinheritance is sound: E001 (P0) gates P0 work; E002 (P1) gates only P1 work (E004,\n55\tBRANCH-B-E006). The P0-slice of HLR-4 in E004 is incidental regression coverage of a\n56\trequirement whose primary delivery is E003 (P0), and the operator-priority tension is\n57\texplicitly raised as a Health Warning requesting human verification — handled correctly.\n58\t\n59\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n60\tAll five DAG edges (E001→E003, E002→E004, E001→BRANCH-A-E005, E001→BRANCH-B-E005,\n61\tE002→BRANCH-B-E006) match the target epics' frontmatter `dependencies` exactly, in the\n62\tdependency→dependent direction consistent with the diagram convention. No circular\n63\tdependencies, no edges to nonexistent epics, and no main-plan epic depends on a branch epic.\n64\tAll three branch files set both `branch` (matching their filename letter) and `gated_by`\n65\t(the gating Investigation), so none will be silently dropped. Parallelism is correct and\n66\tjustified in the DAG Justification table: server (Python), operator (Go), and plugin\n67\t(PyPI package) live in different repositories with no shared build artifacts; the\n68\toperator↔server coupling is a configuration reference (CLI flags rendered into a Deployment\n69\tspec) properly carried as an AC on E004 rather than a `dependencies` edge, and the same\n70\tshape is used for the plugin↔server and BRANCH-B-E006↔E003 couplings — the rule-compliant\n71\tshape, so their absence from the DAG is not a missing data/artifact dependency. No\n72\tkonflux-onboarding, license-validation, or repo-onboarding epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10\n73\tpairings do not apply (validator confirms). Critical path length 2 is short for an M-L\n74\tstrategy but reflects rule-mandated parallelism across the three components rather than\n75\tmissing structure; the depth-2 investigation→implementation chains are complete.\n76\t\n77\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n78\tAll epics carry component `MLflow` (the only canonical entry — verified against\n79\t`.context/rhai-components.txt`, which has no `MLflow Operator` or `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins`\n80\tentries) and team `MLflow Team`, with the mapping constraint logged in the summary and each\n81\tepic's Notes. No cross-team bundling. No scope duplication: the A/B plugin branch epics are\n82\tmutually exclusive alternatives, not parallel builds; E004 (operator-side routing\n83\tpropagation) and BRANCH-B-E006 (server-side delegation surface) split by codebase with the\n84\tboundary explicitly recorded in E004's gate_failure_impact. No work-product type mixing.\n85\tE003 is at the ~2-week guideline (strategy estimates server-side work at 1-2 sprints) but is\n86\tone logical change over a single request-handling surface with the HLR-8 bundling rationale\n87\trecorded — watch note only, no split demanded. E004, however, is sized at 2-3 sprints by the\n88\tstrategy's own estimate (split-deployment topology) with no size Health Warning — see the\n89\tminor issue below.\n90\t\n91\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n92\tBoth Investigations are genuine: E001's decoupled/coupled determination selects between the\n93\ttwo plugin branch epics and rewrites E003's initialization approach; E002's route-level vs.\n94\tserver-delegation determination selects whether BRANCH-B-E006 exists and rewrites E004's\n95\trouting implementation. Both produce concrete decision-record deliverables and both have\n96\tdownstream dependents. All five gated epics have `gated_by` set to an Investigation that\n97\tappears in their direct `dependencies` list, and all have `gate_failure_impact` with both\n98\t`action` (rewrite/remove) and a substantive `fallback_approach` — true gates, not scheduling\n99\tdependencies. No epic lists an Investigation dependency without `gated_by`. Implementation\n100\tepics produce concrete artifacts (server capability, operator topology, plugin changes).\n101\t\n102\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n103\tType-appropriate signal fields throughout: E001/E002 carry `investigation_signals`\n104\t(5-signal rubric), all five Implementation epics carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric), and\n105\tno epic mixes the two. All seven ai-signals rationale files exist and their tables match the\n106\tfrontmatter values exactly. Signal values are well calibrated against the strategy and\n107\tarchitecture context: E002's `local_runnability: 0` (Gateway API routing behavior needs a\n108\tlive cluster) and the branch plugin epics' `repo_access: 0` (plugin source repo not\n109\tdocumented in architecture context — an honest limitation) are appropriately conservative;\n110\tBRANCH-B-E006's `adapter_pattern: 0` (new configuration surface, no reference\n111\timplementation) and BRANCH-B-E005's `change_specificity: 0` (refactor surface known only\n112\tafter the investigation's factoring plan) are justified. `architecture_claims: 1` rationales\n113\tcite the covering architecture-context files (mlflow.md, mlflow-operator.md) rather than\n114\tasserting \"no architecture claims\" — the strategy's premises (flags in the RHOAI container\n115\tentrypoint, Helm-in-operator pattern, conditional CRD discovery) are corroborated, so the\n116\tcalibration check passes. No arithmetic or threshold checking performed, per instructions.\n117\t\n118\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n119\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy: E003's ACs enumerate the exact\n120\tstartup matrix and HTTP response codes (200/403/503) from the strategy's acceptance\n121\tscenarios 1-4; E004's ACs cover strategy scenarios 5-6 plus regression, conditional CRD\n122\tdiscovery, and the misconfiguration-rejection risk mitigation; the branch and Investigation\n123\tepics have document- and behavior-verifiable ACs. No rule-mandated AC is missing: there are\n124\tno replacement epics (backwards-compatibility ACs are present anyway on E003, E004, and\n125\tBRANCH-B-E006), no konflux chain, and no docs-authoring epic (Documentation Support is\n126\t\"Pending human review\", not Yes — Rule 11 correctly not triggered). No externally-controlled\n127\tprecondition is misfiled as an AC: E004's \"rendered artifacts-only instance starts\n128\tsuccessfully with the combined flag set\" gates on a sibling epic within the same\n129\tstrategy/team and is the sanctioned Rule 13 AC-gate coupling, not the soft-AC pattern. No\n130\tepic body references sibling epics by bare draft ID — verified by grep; `E00x`-style\n131\treferences appear only in structured frontmatter fields as full `RHAISTRAT-8009-Exxx` keys.\n132\t\n133\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n134\tThe combined epic set accounts for the full strategy scope: all three affected components,\n135\tall 8 HLRs, and all 6 strategy acceptance scenarios (1-4