{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1a4abdd3b50616b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E006\n3\ttitle: Tracking server artifact-delegation configuration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the split-server routing design investigation resolves routing\n16\t    entirely at the Gateway/HTTPRoute level (outcome A), no tracking-server configuration\n17\t    change is needed and this work falls away; artifact traffic is split at the route\n18\t    without server-side delegation.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Tracking server artifact-delegation configuration\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tBranch epic — outcome B of the split-server artifact traffic routing design investigation (server\n40\tdelegation): routing artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance requires a\n41\tconfiguration change in the MLflow tracking server, not only Gateway/HTTPRoute-level traffic\n42\tsplitting. This epic implements the tracking-server-side configuration that delegates artifact\n43\toperations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, at the functional level characterized by the\n44\tgating investigation. Exact configuration surface naming and format are implementing-team decisions\n45\tinformed by that investigation's design document.\n46\t\n47\tThe configuration must be propagated by the MLflow operator's existing Helm-values mechanisms when\n48\tthe split-server topology is enabled, and its absence must preserve current behavior — a\n49\ttracking server without the delegation configuration serves artifact traffic exactly as it does\n50\ttoday.\n51\t\n52\t## Scope\n53\t\n54\t- Implement the tracking-server configuration that delegates artifact operations to the dedicated\n55\t  artifacts-only instance, per the functional characterization in the gating investigation's design\n56\t  document (what it configures and how the dedicated instance is addressed).\n57\t- Ensure the configuration is settable through the mechanisms the operator already uses to\n58\t  configure the main tracking deployment, so the split-server topology can propagate it from a\n59\t  single MLflow CR.\n60\t- Backwards compatibility: absent configuration, the tracking server's artifact handling retains\n61\t  current behavior; no existing API contracts, CLI arguments, or configuration keys change meaning.\n62\t- Test coverage: delegation active (artifact operations routed to the configured dedicated\n63\t  instance), delegation absent (current behavior), and interaction with workspace-aware\n64\t  artifacts-only serving (delegated requests remain subject to workspace validation at the\n65\t  dedicated instance).\n66\t\n67\t## Acceptance Criteria\n68\t\n69\t- A tracking server configured with the artifact-delegation configuration delegates artifact\n70\t  operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, verified by artifact requests being served\n71\t  through the dedicated instance.\n72\t- A tracking server without the delegation configuration serves artifact traffic exactly as before\n73\t  (current behavior preserved, regression suite green).\n74\t- The configuration is consumable by the operator's existing configuration-propagation mechanisms\n75\t  for the main tracking deployment.\n76\t- Artifact requests delegated to the dedicated instance remain subject to workspace validation at\n77\t  that instance (end-to-end through the split topology).\n78\t- The configuration surface is documented for administrators of multi-tenant deployments.\n79\t\n80\t## HLR Traceability\n81\t\n82\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only\n83\t  instance — this epic delivers the server-side half of that routing under outcome B of the gating\n84\t  investigation (the operator-side routing configuration is delivered by the split-server operator\n85\t  topology work).\n86\t\n87\t## Notes\n88\t\n89\t- This branch epic exists only if the split-server routing design investigation determines outcome B\n90\t  (the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations). Under outcome\n91\t  A (route-level traffic splitting at the Gateway/HTTPRoute layer), no tracking-server change is\n92\t  needed and this work falls away.\n93\t- Builds on the workspace-aware artifacts-only serving capability delivered by the server-side\n94\t  combined-flag work; delegated artifact requests are validated at the dedicated instance by that\n95\t  capability.\n96\t- Component mapping: canonical Jira component `MLflow`.\n97\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a78bd5ae81820315","agent_id":"ae780ac218091a484","session_id":"16006724-b396-4d55-996f-e395dcbbe214","uuid":"09724bdf-7c32-465e-a8c2-278e30ebb731","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:47:23.694Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1a4abdd3b50616b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
