{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-974f5ede9c5410ba","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AI Signals Rationale: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003 (Implementation)\n2\t\n3\tImplementation epic — scored with the 9 implementation signals.\n4\t\n5\t| Signal | Value | Rationale |\n6\t|---|---|---|\n7\t| change_specificity | +1 | The strategy specifies exact flags (`--artifacts-only`, `--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`), the artifact path structure (`{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`), the endpoint family (`/api/2.0/mlflow/artifacts/*`), and exact response codes (200/403/503) for each scenario. |\n8\t| pattern_precedent | +1 | Workspace validation already runs in the same codebase for non-artifact operations (`--enable-workspaces`, kubernetes-auth plugin, workspace store), and an artifacts-only serving mode already exists; this epic composes existing patterns rather than inventing new ones. |\n9\t| adapter_pattern | +1 | Authorization delegation follows the existing auth plugin infrastructure (entry-point-loaded kubernetes-auth plugin via `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`), the same reference implementation the tracking server uses for workspace-scoped authorization (mlflow.md). |\n10\t| existing_foundation | +1 | Extends existing flags, an existing artifacts-only mode, and an existing workspace store — no greenfield surface. |\n11\t| open_questions | -1 | Gated on the workspace-resolution initialization-dependency investigation: whether the workspace provider can be initialized without tracking/model registry stores changes this epic's initialization approach (rewrite gate). |\n12\t| external_dependency | 0 | No upstream contribution or vendor coordination: the server repo and the plugin package are both MLflow Team-owned; the workspace store, Gateway API, and kube-rbac-proxy all exist in the platform. |\n13\t| human_process_gates | -1 | The strategy's prerequisites list Architecture Review, ODH/RHOAI Build Onboarding, and License Validation as \"Pending human review\", and the acceptance criteria are explicitly marked as requiring PM/Engineering validation — human approval steps precede implementation. |\n14\t| repo_access | +1 | The target repo (red-hat-data-services/mlflow, per mlflow.md) is a readable Git repository the implementing agent can clone and modify. |\n15\t| architecture_claims | +1 | The strategy's premises are corroborated by the architecture context: mlflow.md documents the `--app-name kubernetes-auth` / `--enable-workspaces` / `--workspace-store-uri kubernetes://` flags in the RHOAI container entrypoint (Dockerfile.konflux CMD), the kubernetes-auth plugin from mlflow-kubernetes-plugins v1.5.0, and the workspace-isolation model this epic extends. |\n16\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a78bd5ae81820315","agent_id":"ae780ac218091a484","session_id":"16006724-b396-4d55-996f-e395dcbbe214","uuid":"2fb9a012-180b-4928-b940-616062491a5b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:47:32.508Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-974f5ede9c5410ba","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
